    <paragraph>For the following exercises, $$P$$ is a point on the unit circle. a. Find the (exact) missing coordinate value of each point and b. find the values of the six trigonometric functions for the angle $$\theta$$ with a terminal side that passes through point $$P.$$ Rationalize denominators.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="135" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$P\left( {\frac{7}{25},y} \right),y &gt; 0$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>a. $$y=2425y=2425$$ b. $$sin\theta =2425,cos\theta =725,tan\theta =247,csc\theta =2524,sec\theta =257,cot\theta =724sin\theta =2425,cos\theta =725,tan\theta =247,csc\theta =2524,sec\theta =257,cot\theta =724$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="136" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$P\left( {\frac{-15}{17},y} \right),y &lt; 0$$</paragraph>
